---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import headshot from '../assets/headshot.jpg';
---

<Layout
  title="About | Joe Fazio"
  description="Joe Fazio: JMU Computer Information Systems graduate focused on mastering IT fundamentals and helping businesses stay secure."
>
  <div class="cols">
    <div class="side">
      <div class="block">
        <Image
          src={headshot}
          alt="Joe Fazio."
          widths={[280, 560]}
          sizes="(max-width: 40rem) 15rem, 14rem"
          loading="eager"
        />
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="text">
      <h1>About</h1>

      <p>
        I'm Joe. I graduated from James Madison University with a degree in
        Computer Information Systems from the College of Business.
      </p>

      <p>
        I want to master the fundamentals of IT and help businesses stay secure.
        Support, systems, networking, cloud, and security all build on each
        other, so I'm open to any of them. Every role teaches something that
        makes me better at the rest.
      </p>

      <p>
        The two things worth knowing about how I work: I am reliable and I am
        persistent. I finish what I pick up, and I stay on a problem past the point
        where it stops being interesting.
      </p>

      <h2>What I'm building</h2>

      <p>
        This site. The infrastructure is the point: Astro, Cloudflare Pages, DNS I
        manage myself, and a build in GitHub Actions that has to pass before anything
        reaches the main branch. The repository is public and every choice in it has
        a written reason attached, including the ones I got wrong and went back to
        fix. I wanted infrastructure I could explain out loud.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* Photo in its own column beside the text. On a wide screen it stays in
     view while the text scrolls; on a phone it sits above the text. */
  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 14rem 1fr;
    gap: 2.25rem;
    align-items: start;
  }

  .side {
    position: sticky;
    top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .text h1 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  /* A block of color sits offset behind the photo, the same off-register
     look as the Record Store sleeves. */
  .block {
    position: relative;
    margin: 0.4rem 1rem 1rem 0;
  }

  .block::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    transform: translate(1rem, 1rem);
    border-radius: 6px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 70% 30%, rgb(224 169 46 / 0.6), transparent 60%),
      #9a5f97;
  }

  .block :global(img) {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 6px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.3);
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }

    .side {
      position: static;
      max-width: 15rem;
    }
  }
</style>
